    "interpretation": {
      "regularRedirect": "exec perfetto ... -c - < /data/local/tmp/config opens the regular file while still in the shell domain, then inherits it into perfetto. fd use alone does not authorize reading its shell_data_file inode. The reviewed domain/global/perfetto rules provide no such inode read grant; device-specific compiled policy was not exhaustively reconstructed.",
      "whyEmptyPossible": "The reference kernel explicitly revalidates inherited descriptors on the domain transition and substitutes a null file for unauthorized ones. This provides a source-supported possible route from a nonempty verified remote regular file to empty stdin. No AVC, errno, runtime descriptor target or policy dump was collected for run41580632157, so this is not a proven attribution of that observed failure.",
      "supportedInputs": "Host stdin over the adb stream, or a shell-created pipe, has explicit reviewed permissions. A config under /data/misc/perfetto-configs also has explicit regular-file read permission. Retain source/path/hash and actual CLI result checks; do not add root, relabel files, change policy or use hidden exemptions.",
      "signalLiveness": "SIGINT permission is explicit; kill -0 needs a separate signull permission not found in the reviewed shell/domain/perfetto rules. Do not equate a nonzero kill -0 result with absence of the process. Prefer bounded proc identity reads and separate missing/unreadable states.",
      "procIdentity": "Read-only stat/comm/cmdline is supported by reviewed shell domain-file permissions, assuming normal proc labels and applicable DAC/procfs controls. This is not proof that every field will be visible on the runtime image.",
      "traceOutput": "Reviewed policy permits perfetto creation and shell cat/stat/hash/unlink within /data/misc/perfetto-traces; shell is not granted trace-content modification by the cited rule. Directory/file labels, DAC ownership/mode, and runtime results remain independently checked."
    },
    "limits": [
      "No repository files or device state were changed.",
      "The Android17 policy tag exists and is pinned; no moving HEAD was used for policy conclusions.",
      "The kernel reference is a separate pinned branch commit, not asserted to match the emulator.",
      "No entire policy repository was downloaded or built; absence of an allow in reviewed files is not a compiled policy proof.",
      "Policy source and file hashes do not establish the errno or fd disposition in the failed run."
    ]
  },
  "pipeFixReview": {
    "command": "adb -s <recorded-serial> shell /system/bin/perfetto --txt -c - -o <unique-owned-trace-path> --background-wait",
    "delivery": "Popen stdin=PIPE, binary/unbuffered and nonblocking; exact local frozen config bytes are written with selectors while merged stdout/stderr is drained under the same original 15-second deadline. No inherited regular configuration fd remains in the launch path.",
    "receipt": "The command receipt binds trace-config.pbtxt bytes/SHA-256, actual successful host write count, and EOF closure. Start command admission, owner admission, and recorded receipt validation require exact config identity, full writtenBytes, eofSent=true, completed status, and exit 0. Host pipe writes do not establish device consumption by themselves.",
    "failureBoundaries": "Partial/no-EOF delivery, write error, command exception, timeout, cancellation, output truncation, and exit 1 remain unsuccessful. PID-shaped output cannot bypass start admission; failed/unowned start cannot signal a device PID or enter A/B.",
    "hostCleanup": "The new input process is started in its own session. Finally attempts SIGKILL on that local group even if its leader has exited, handling ESRCH and retaining other cleanup errors; streams close and child wait remains bounded. This covers a descendant holding stdout after leader exit. This host cleanup is distinct from the separately owned remote Perfetto SIGINT stop.",
    "remoteOwnership": "Native printed PID is followed by positive start ticks, comm=perfetto, and exact NUL-delimited cmdline. Before the single SIGINT, current start ticks and exact command line are checked again; the finite shell rechecks comm/ticks/cmdline hash immediately before signalling. PID/start-time checks are not an atomic pidfd operation.",
    "procAndSignal": "Pinned Android17 policy permits shell reads of domain proc files and SIGINT-style signal to perfetto; signull/kill -0 is a distinct permission and is not used. Actual runtime proc fields/exit/trace-file permissions still require direct command success.",
    "stopAndFile": "SIGINT is a supported graceful stop in the reference implementation. Exit confirmation, regular/non-symlink file, bounded nonempty size, byte-complete pull, SHA-256, and cleanup remain required independently. Early exit or PID reuse is preserved as unverified; there is no global kill or root.",
    "unchangedBudgets": "Raw/keyboard implementation, each original 12-second arm and one-show contract, trace 120-second/32-MiB limits, command budgets, generic non-help exit-0 requirement, and separate setting restoration before own trace stop are unchanged. The reviewed producer binding has 25 unchanged files and only the new wrapper differs.",
